  "goodToKnow": "Jedermann means everybody and sounds formal: Das Angebot steht jedermann offen. The genitive is jedermanns: Das ist nicht jedermanns Sache. It's still common in official language and in set phrases, though gender-neutral alternatives like alle are growing. Jedermann is also the title of Hugo von Hofmannsthal's play, performed in front of Salzburg Cathedral every summer since the Salzburg Festival began in 1920."
